{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>But evil shall come upon you.</b> A day of evil." "<b>You shall not know its dawn.</b> Like a night that has no dawn, and the meaning is light." "<b>It shall come.</b> From the root of ואתה הוה להם (Nehemiah 6:6), in the sense of evil that comes suddenly, and like it: והותי במאזנים (Job 6:2)." "<b>To appease it.</b> To give a ransom to remove it or to annul it, like ואיש חכם יכפרנה (Proverbs 16:14)." "<b>Destruction.</b> Like desolation."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:27.314068785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}